Flexbox lays items out in a row or column:
```css
.row {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;          /* or column */
  justify-content: space-between; /* along the main axis */
  align-items: center;          /* across */
  gap: 12px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;              /* wrap on small screens */
}
.item { flex: 1; }              /* share space equally */
```

Grid lays items out in rows and columns:
```css
.gallery {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));  /* responsive columns */
  gap: 16px;
}
.wide { grid-column: span 2; }
```

1) Add `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">`. 2) Use flexbox/grid and percentages or `min()` instead of fixed widths. 3) Use media queries:
```css
.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
@media (max-width: 700px) {
  .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }   /* one column on phones */
}
img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
```

